                             c_{i+1 \\\\pmod L}$.\\nSo $g^a(c_0) =              
                             c_{a \\\\pmod L}$.\\nThus, $a \\\\pmod             
                             L$ is the index $j$ such that $A(c_0) =            
                             c_j$.\\n\\nLet\'s try this.\\nI\'ll                
                             need to parse the output first."\n                 
